      "Language": "ukr",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "In the article the concentration of endothelin-1 in patients with different variants of APS was analyzed and its relationship with disease course, dyslipidemia, levels of antiphospholipid antibodies and ath rosclerotic vascular lesions was assessed. It was established that high levels of endothelin-1 is a circulating marker of early atherosclerosis, since !it was closely associated'with subclinical manifestations of atherosclerotic vascular lesions, lipid profile. The concentration of endothelin-1 significantly increased with active inflammation and with high levels of antiphospholipid antibodies and does not depend on age, sex, smoking, obesity and physical inactivity."},
